    "title": "Chipotle BOGO tattoo deal: How to get a free burrito on Friday",
    "text": "Chipotle announced it will offer a one-hour buy-one-get-one promotion on March 13 for customers who show up to restaurants with any tattoos. (Photo by: Jeffrey Greenberg/Universal Images Group via Getty Images)Jeff Greenberg/Jeffrey Greenberg/Universal ImagGot any tats you can show off? It can get you some free lunch. Watch MoreChipotle announced its “tatted like a Chipotle bag” buy-one-get-one promotion scheduled for a one-hour window on March 13 for customers who show up to restaurants with any tattoos.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢The promotion will run from 3 to 4 p.m. local time at participating locations in the U.S., Canada, the United Kingdom, France and Germany.Chipotle partnered with multi-platinum hip-hop artist Swae Lee of Rae Sremmurd to co-design an exclusive temporary tattoo flash sheet, drawing inspiration from the artwork featured on Chipotle’s takeout bags.“'Tatted like a Chipotle bag' is really about self-expression,” Lee said. “It was cool to bring it into the real world and create designs that actually feel like me.”Here's what to know about the promotion. Article continues below this adDoes it have to be a permanent tattoo?It doesn't matter what kind of ink you have. Customers with any kind of tattoo — whether it's permanent, temporary or drawn-on — can get the BOGO offer during the one-hour window. Article continues below this adThe promotion takes its inspiration from the Friday the 13th “flash tattoo” tradition, where tattoo shops offer sheets of small, pre-designed tattoos in celebration of the day.“What started as an internet meme became a real-world expression of fandom for our brand,” Stephanie Perdue, Chipotle’s interim chief marketing officer said.Chipotle said a similar tattoo-themed buy-one-get-one promotion in June 2025 drove the company’s highest mid-afternoon sales on record.Article continues below this adThe March 13 offer is valid for in-restaurant purchases only and requires customers to buy an entrée of equal or greater value to receive a free item. Additional restrictions may apply, according to the company.March 11, 2026Trending ReporterMarley Malenfant is a 10-year multimedia journalist who’s worked in print, digital, and broadcast. His prior work includes working in West Texas as a TV reporter for KTXS. During his time there, he covered education, sports, features, and breaking News. He’s skilled in front of the camera as well as behind it. He was a freelance writer, published in D Magazine, Dallas Morning News, SB Nation, Dallas Observer, and was a personality for “The Coach Brothers” sports radio show. Outside of journalism, he was an educator in the Dallas area. He was a 2012 Mayborn Literary Nonfiction Conference grant recipient. In 2021, he was part of the NABJ student multimedia project. He graduated with a paralegal degree from El Centro in 2023. Currently, he’s a trending news reporter for the Austin American-Statesman, covering breaking News, sports, music, and legal trends.",
